## Hard Decisions

- Inter-VLAN traffic is default deny.
- `{{ dns.zone }}` is the internal DNS suffix.
- AdGuard Home in `VLAN {{ (zones | selectattr('id', 'equalto', 'server') | first).vlan }}` is the primary internal resolver.
- Tailscale uses `{{ tailnet.policy_model }}`, not new ACL work.
- Linux edge and server nodes use Tailscale SSH for admin access. Public SSH stays closed.
- Remote NAS storage is allowed over the tailnet for approved users. `SMB` is the remote file protocol. `NFS` stays internal.
- The Tailscale subnet router lives on a dedicated server-side node, not on the Flint 2.
- Edge servers join the tailnet. Private naming there uses MagicDNS and the private `{{ dns.private_tailnet_domain.zone }}` zone, while `{{ dns.zone }}` stays the split-DNS namespace for homelab services.
- `{{ tailnet.edge_publishing.public_domain }}` terminates on an edge reverse proxy that joins the tailnet. Public app exposure uses Tailscale as the backhaul, not as the browser-facing DNS or certificate layer.
- Tailnet-only apps use `*.{{ dns.private_tailnet_domain.zone }}` instead of `*.ts.net` names. That is private network gating by Tailscale grants, not a substitute for app auth on sensitive services.
- Tailscale Funnel is out of scope for this design.
- The GL-S200 stays on GL.iNet firmware. Its management plane is on `VLAN 99`. Its IoT SSID bridges into `VLAN 30`.

